{"key":"enterprise/T1036.010","id":"T1036.010","name":"Masquerade Account Name","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1036","tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["Containers","IaaS","Identity Provider","Linux","macOS","Office Suite","SaaS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud","cloud-hosted-endpoint","containers","identity","onprem","saas"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may match or approximate the names of legitimate accounts to make newly created ones appear benign. This will typically occur during Create Account, although accounts may also be renamed at a later date. This may also coincide with Account Access Removal if the actor first deletes an account before re-creating one with the same name. Often, adversaries will attempt to masquerade as service accounts, such as those associated with…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1036/010","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--d349c66e-18e1-4d8b-a2d7-65af7cbd2ba0","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.717Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0014","name":"User Account Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0014","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--deb22295-7e37-4a3b-ac6f-c86666fbe63d","page":"telemetry/DC0014/"},{"id":"DC0013","name":"User Account Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0013","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--b5d0492b-cda4-421c-8e51-ed2b8d85c5d0","page":"telemetry/DC0013/"},{"id":"DC0010","name":"User Account Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0010","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--d27b0089-2c39-4b6c-84ff-303e48657e77","page":"telemetry/DC0010/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0383","name":"Detection Strategy for Masquerading via Account Name Similarity","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0383","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--f1f9b6fc-a261-4bcf-a0c0-3ae42cdc28fc","relationship_id":"relationship--8a466394-34b7-4836-9876-70dfeb30836d"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1077","name":"Analytic 1077","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0383#AN1077","guidance":"Detects adversary behavior where a newly created or renamed user account closely resembles existing service or administrator accounts to blend in and avoid detection. Common patterns include prefix/suffix modifications, homoglyphs, or use of names like 'admin1', 'adm1n', or 'backup_help'.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0383"},{"id":"AN1078","name":"Analytic 1078","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0383#AN1078","guidance":"Detects creation or renaming of accounts with names that closely match known service, root, or admin accounts. Behavior often follows account discovery or deletion, attempting to blend into system activity logs using trusted name conventions.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0383"},{"id":"AN1079","name":"Analytic 1079","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0383#AN1079","guidance":"Detects adversary creation of cloud or IdP accounts whose names resemble existing privileged or service accounts. May indicate preparation for privilege escalation or defense evasion.","platforms":["Identity Provider"],"strategy_id":"DET0383"},{"id":"AN1080","name":"Analytic 1080","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0383#AN1080","guidance":"Monitors for the creation of accounts inside containers using names that resemble legitimate orchestrator or backup identities to mask adversary persistence.","platforms":["Containers"],"strategy_id":"DET0383"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0014","component":"User Account Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4720","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1077","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0383#AN1077","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0014/"},{"component_id":"DC00